to worship, adore, honour (esp. with sacrifice or oblations);
to consecrate, hallow, offer (with acc., rarely dat. loc. or प्रति, of the deity or person to whom; dat. of the person for whom, or the thing for which; and instr. of the means by which the sacrifice is performed; in older language generally P. of Agni or any other mediator, and Ā. of one who makes an offering on his own account, cf. य॑ज-मान; later properly P. when used with reference to the officiating priest, and Ā. when referring to the institutor of the sacrifice), RV. &c. &c.;
